 PDF extraction – root cause found
  ▎
  ▎ How it works: we base64-encode the PDF and send it via the MID server to Chinou's /invoke endpoint — the same one used for text calls. Chinou decodes it, reads the document,
  ▎ returns cashflow rows. The base64 step is lossless; we verified the bytes arrive intact.
  ▎
  ▎ Finding: Chinou's document reader returns HTTP 200 with an empty body for any PDF whose fonts are not embedded. Confirmed across 5 such PDFs, 20 attempts, zero characters ever
  ▎ returned. PDFs that embed fonts, and scanned PDFs, read reliably on the same endpoint in the same session.
  ▎
  ▎ Scope: 10 of the 26 PDFs in the corpus are non-embedded-font — all produced by Smart Communications SC27 or PD4ML HTML-to-PDF. Business impact is limited to the 8 mails where
  ▎ the PDF is the only source of the figures; the rest carry their trade in the mail body and are unaffected.
  ▎
  ▎ Ruled out: our code, the payload (byte-verified), the prompt (fails even with no field spec), OCR (all have text layers), and flakiness (0/5 vs 5/5 on identical repeated
  ▎ calls).
  ▎
  ▎ Next: testing Chinou's dedicated document parser on port 9060 (chinou-doc-parser-stg…:9060/invoke) — we've never used it; our calls go to the base text gateway. If it renders
  ▎ rather than extracts, it should handle these. URL change only. If not, this goes to the Chinou team — evidence is ready
